### 3. Insert Your CSS

- Inside the editor, you’ll see a pre-filled keyword selector.
- Use *selector* as a placeholder. It automatically maps to the **current block** you’re editing.

Example:

```
selector {
    background-color: #f5f5f5;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 20px;
}
```

This ensures that your CSS only applies to the selected block, without affecting other elements on the page.![](https://res.cloudinary.com/lwcom/images/w_381,h_1024,c_scale/f_auto,q_auto/v1780352329/prod/image_4606251c846/image_4606251c846.png?_i=AA)

